course: dictionary
lesson: 14890
title: Recommence: starting again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long and formal, but you can often work out their meaning from their parts. Recommence has two parts: re- means again, and commence means begin. Put them together and recommence means begin again.
explain: «After the lunch break, the lessons will recommence at two o'clock.» The lessons had stopped for lunch, and now they start again. The clue is the word break, which tells you there was a stop first.
explain: Recommence is a formal word. You will often see it in notices, on the news, or in exam papers, but in everyday talk people usually say start again or resume. If you read recommence in a story, you can swap in start again and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Recommence is a verb. It means to begin again after a stop or break, or to start doing something again.
fact: The word is made from re- (again) and commence (begin).
fact: «Lessons will recommence on Monday.» This means lessons begin again after the holiday.
fact: Everyday words with the same meaning include start again and resume. Recommence sounds more formal and official.
fact: Useful phrases with recommence are work recommenced, recommence play, and recommence lessons.
exercise: «After the lunch break, the lessons will recommence at two o'clock.» What does recommence mean here? | Move to a new classroom | Eat lunch more slowly | *Begin again after a break | Finish for the whole day
exercise: The word recommence is made of re- (again) and commence (begin). What does recommence mean? | To run very fast | *To start again | To read a book quietly | To stop forever
exercise: «The rain stopped, and the football match recommenced.» Which everyday word could replace recommenced? | hid | finished | forgot | *resumed
test: Which phrase means the same as recommence? | Sit down quietly | *Start again | Go home early | Never begin
test: In which notice would you most likely see the word recommence? | Please pass the salt. | I love my new red bike. | *Lessons will recommence on Monday. | Let's play tag at the park!
exam: «The band recommenced playing after the interval.» What does this tell you? | The band never played at all | The band stopped playing for ever | *The band started again after a stop | The band started for the very first time
